  "id": "implicit-behavior",
  "term": "implicit behavior",
  "definition": "Implicit behavior is a person’s performance in a task that reveals psychological processing indirectly, rather than through their own stated judgment about it. In this source, it refers to behavior in an experimental emotion-recognition task that can show emotional processing difficulties even when the person does not report such problems explicitly.",
